%% Azure Data Box seed - order states, the copy rules that decide whether the seed is usable, and the File Sync attach decision - Contoso profile
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Tutorial to return Azure Data Box" (order states, prepare to ship, CRC check, NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1 erasure, 14-day auto-complete), "Migrate data into Azure File Sync with Azure Data Box" (SMB only, first-level folder mapping, 10 storage accounts per appliance, authoritative upload rules)
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Ordered

  state "Ordered - the target storage accounts are named on the order" as Ordered
  note right of Ordered
    One appliance can feed at most 10 storage accounts.
    Never split one file share across two appliances.
    Data Box Disk is excluded for Azure file shares because
    it does not preserve file metadata.
  end note

  state "Delivered and unlocked on Contoso LAN" as Delivered
  Ordered --> Delivered : carrier transit, plan one to two weeks each way

  state Copying {
    [*] --> ShareLayout
    state "Write into the account underscore AzFile SMB share only" as ShareLayout
    state "One first-level folder per source share - the folder name becomes the Azure file share name" as FolderRule
    state "robocopy /MT /R /W /B /MIR /IT /COPY DATSO /DCOPY DAT into that folder" as Copy
    ShareLayout --> FolderRule : ignore the block and page blob shares on the same device
    FolderRule --> Copy
    Copy --> [*] : copy log clean
  }
  Delivered --> Copying
  note left of Copying
    Only SMB copy is supported for Data Box and Data Box Heavy.
    The data copy service is not usable here because it does not
    preserve file fidelity. Files written to the root of the
    AzFile share instead of a first-level folder are not ingested.
  end note

  state "Prepare to ship - device validation, reference number and shipping label" as Prepare
  Copying --> Prepare
  Prepare --> Copying : validation errors, fix and re-run
  state "Picked up - carrier scan, tracking id in the portal" as PickedUp
  Prepare --> PickedUp : prepare to ship succeeded

  state "Received - physical inspection at the Azure datacenter" as Received
  PickedUp --> Received
  state "Data copy in progress - upload runs, CRC compared against the copy" as Uploading
  Received --> Uploading

  state "Completed" as Completed
  state "Data copy completed with errors, device pending data erasure" as WithErrors
  Uploading --> Completed : every file uploaded and the CRCs match
  Uploading --> WithErrors : non-retryable errors in the copy log
  WithErrors --> ErasedWithErrors : operator confirms device erasure, or the order auto-completes after 14 days
  state "Copy completed with errors - the missed files must be moved by wire" as ErasedWithErrors

  state "Secure erase to NIST SP 800-88 Revision 1" as Erased
  Completed --> Erased
  ErasedWithErrors --> Erased

  state HierarchyCheck <<choice>>
  Completed --> HierarchyCheck : now attach Azure File Sync to the seeded share
  HierarchyCheck --> Authoritative : the server path matches the seeded hierarchy exactly
  HierarchyCheck --> Merge : any mismatch, or the share already has another server endpoint

  state "Initial upload ServerAuthoritative - only available on the FIRST server endpoint in the sync group" as Authoritative
  state "Initial upload Merge - conflicting files are kept side by side" as Merge
  state "Seed realised - only the changes since the copy travel over ExpressRoute" as Seeded
  state "Seed destroyed - the Azure file share is emptied and re-uploaded in full from the server" as Wasted
  Authoritative --> Seeded : hierarchy verified before the endpoint was created
  Authoritative --> Wasted : hierarchy was not verified
  Merge --> Seeded : slower reconciliation, no data loss
  Seeded --> [*]
  Wasted --> [*]
  Erased --> [*]
